// @error cannot assign i32 to 'z' of type Z
// CONTRACT (must-REJECT): softening a numeric literal-union ALIAS to its base scalar at
// EMIT (`literal-unions/numeric-litunion-alias.vl`) must not soften it in the CHECKER.
// `5` is not a member of `0 | 1`, and the emit-side vocabulary rewrite happens in
// `canonEmitTypeNames` — at the END of `checkProgram`, after every membership decision.
//
// The companion positions (assignment, argument, return, field, element) were graded the
// same way and reject identically on both sides; this file pins the initializer, the one
// the fix's own repro used.
//
// HONESTLY: this is a CONTROL, not a red-on-parent pin. It passes on the parent commit
// too — that is the point, the fix must not move it. It is entombed by SABOTAGE instead:
// routing `numLitUnionAliasName` through the checker's resolution (`nameToTy`) rather than
// only through `canonEmitName` makes this file compile and print 5.
type Z = 0 | 1
const z: Z = 5
print(z)
